 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for committed changes.** Fast updates and freedom from realtime-provider coupling justify operating connection capacity and reconnect recovery. Five-second HTTPS polling offers simpler stateless operation but adds repeated reads and several seconds of lag. A hosted realtime service reduces connection operations but introduces recurring fees and provider coupling. Both can meet the 15-second freshness goal. See [Delivery of committed board changes](decisions/change-delivery.md).
